{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The events’ Swift types are the source of their schema. A tracking plan, the JSON Schema (draft"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2020-12) of every event an app tracks, is exported from them for the people and tools outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app. "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own that "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves out) turns schemas into the plan’s files, one document per event and an index, as values:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import TrackingPlans","","let plan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [CheckoutStarted.schema])","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.schema.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.example.json\"]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bytes depend on the schemas alone: keys sorted, two-space indentation, a trailing newline and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no timestamps, the same on every run and platform, so the plan can be committed and reviewed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"What each document says","anchor":"What-each-document-says","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each document requires the properties that are neither optional nor have a default value, allows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the optional ones, and rejects any other property. It carries the event’s version and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category (","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-consent-category","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is marked ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one with a default value is marked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and isn’t required, since an earlier release’s payload lacks it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property removed at the same version stays in the document with the schema it had, marked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deprecated"},{"type":"text","text":" and not required, so the payloads of releases that still send it validate: exporting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over the committed plan carries it forward. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":"’s documentation lists how each Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type maps."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beside each document is the event’s example, a conformance vector: the payload with every property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to a fixed value its schema accepts (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"example\""},{"text":", 0, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":", one array element). Another","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform’s client can encode the same event and compare it against the example.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Exporting the plan","anchor":"Exporting-the-plan","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tool can only read the schemas of types it is compiled against, so the plan is written by a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable in your package that lists your events:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".executableTarget(name: \"AppTrackingPlan\", dependencies: [","    \"AppEvents\",","    .product(name: \"TrackingPlans\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","]),"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The example package’s executable, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StoreTrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":", is one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import StoreEvents","import TrackingPlans","","\/\/\/ Writes the store's tracking plan: `swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory","\/\/\/ export-tracking-plan`, from Examples\/, writes it into Examples\/TrackingPlan.","@main","struct StoreTrackingPlan: TrackingPlanCommand {","    static let trackingPlan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [","        CheckoutStarted.schema,","        OrderCompleted.schema,","        SignedUp.schema,","    ])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then one command, run from the package’s directory, builds it and writes the plan into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan\/"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"sh","code":["swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory export-tracking-plan"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"text":" plugin runs the package’s one executable target that depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--product <name>"},{"text":" picks one of several, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--output <directory>"},{"text":" writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere in the package. Writing again deletes the documents of events the plan no longer lists.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the plan ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StoreTrackingPlan"},{"text":" writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Checking the plan","anchor":"Checking-the-plan","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The committed plan is the contract every platform that sends the events agrees on. One command","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails when the Swift events no longer match it, with a line naming each event and property that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"sh","code":["swift package check-tracking-plan"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A difference is breaking when, at the same version, a record a store still holds or a payload an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already released app sends may stop decoding or validating:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a removed or renamed event;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a retyped property;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"an optional property made required;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a new required property without a default value;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a default value removed;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a deprecated property declared again with another type, or as required."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anything else leaves the committed plan out of date, which fails with its own message telling you to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export it again: a new event, a new optional property or one with a default value, a removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, a deprecated one declared again as it was, or a changed consent category."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A constraint is compared keyword by keyword. Tightening one is breaking: a higher "},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a lower "},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a new bound, a new or changed "},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Loosening one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only leaves the plan out of date. An integer type narrowed to one of fewer bits tightens its bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same way. Raising an event’s version ("},{"code":"@Event(version: 3)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") is how a breaking change is made on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"purpose: the new version gets a document of its own. "},{"code":"--plan <directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" checks a plan committed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elsewhere, and "},{"code":"--product <name>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" picks the executable, as it does for export."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Checking from a test","anchor":"Checking-from-a-test","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same check runs from a test, so it runs wherever the app’s tests do. Add the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},{"text":" product to a test target that depends on the executable, as the example","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"package’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"StoreTrackingPlanTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Foundation","@testable import StoreTrackingPlan","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Suite(\"StoreTrackingPlan\")","struct StoreTrackingPlanTests {","    @Test(\"The store's events match its committed tracking plan\")","    func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() {","        let plan = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","            .deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent()","            .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","        expectTrackingPlan(StoreTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: plan)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It records an issue with the report the command prints. ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.check(against:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same comparison as a value, each ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlanDifference","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with whether it ","type":"text"},{"code":"isBreaking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"https://github.com/Tyler-Keith-Thompson/Traffluent/tree/main/Examples/TrackingPlan":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","type":"link","title":"Examples\/TrackingPlan","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"Examples\/TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","title":"Defining Events","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"title":"Consent Gating","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"title":"Sampling Events","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"title":"Traffluent","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks as a tracking plan, and check the events against the plan committed before them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","title":"TrackingPlans","role":"collection"}}}